{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788133114,"nonce":"23v/ImpSAcSAKMkgfHKGuCssnqY=","message":"PRESERVED RESEARCH — pawn read-safety catalogue, session 4.\n\nA sub-agent of the stopped 2.2 worker returned this after the parent was killed.\nIt is the most valuable artifact either produced and re-deriving it would cost\nanother opus run, so it is recorded here verbatim in substance. **Leads to\nverify, not established fact** — no code was ever run against it, and I have\nspot-checked only what is noted at the end.\n\n\n| Accessor | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `Pawn_WorkSettings.GetPriority` / `WorkIsActive` WITHOUT an `EverWork` guard | `ConfirmInitializedDebug` -\u003e `EnableAndInitialize` **rewrites the pawn's work priorities** and logs an error |\n| `Pawn_WorkSettings.WorkGiversInOrder{Normal,Emergency}` | rebuilds instance lists + the **static** `wtsByPrio` |\n| `Pawn_PlayerSettings.EffectiveAreaRestrictionInPawnCurrentMap` | `Dictionary.TryGetValue(null)` **throws** for caravan/pod pawns (missing null guard the sibling getter has) |\n| `Pawn_RelationsTracker.OpinionOf` | creates `CachedSocialThoughts` entries + `Thought_SituationalSocial` objects, stamps `lastQueryTick`; **plus a full family BFS per call** |\n| `Pawn_RelationsTracker.RelatedPawns` abandoned mid-enumeration | leaves `canCacheFamilyByBlood == true` and a stale cache **permanently** |\n| `SocialCardUtility.*` except `GetPawnSituationLabel` | static `cachedForPawn`/`cachedEntries`; `PawnsForSocialInfo` returns a cleared-and-refilled **shared static** |\n| `TraitSet.TraitsSorted` (retained) | cleared/refilled per-instance tmp list |\n| `WorkTypeDef.VisibleCurrently` | writes a frame cache, walks `PawnsFinder` |\n| `Pawn_IdeoTracker.Certainty` on a baby | **writes `certaintyInt` from the getter** (a Scribe-serialized field) |\n| anything reaching `Pawn_AgeTracker.CurLifeStageIndex` on a cold pawn | lazy-creates `Pawn.Drawer`, **can rename the pawn**, rebuilds trackers |\n\n\n**1. `Pawn_WorkSettings.GetPriority` MUTATES.** `RimWorld/Pawn_WorkSettings.cs:160`\ncalls `ConfirmInitializedDebug()` (`:131`), which on `priorities == null` logs an\nerror AND calls `EnableAndInitialize()` (`:89-129`) — allocating a `DefMap` and\ncalling `SetPriority` up to 6 times, each of which can call\n`pawn.jobs.Notify_WorkTypeDisabled`. **So reading a work priority off a pawn that\nnever had work settings permanently rewrites that pawn's priorities.**\nCorrect gate, and the one vanilla itself uses at\n`PawnColumnWorker_WorkPriority.cs:20`:\n`pawn.workSettings != null \u0026\u0026 pawn.workSettings.EverWork`.\nAlso: `GetPriority` returns **3 for every active work type** when\n`Find.PlaySettings.useWorkPriorities` is off — the number you serialize is not\nthe stored number, so record that flag alongside it.\n\n**2. `OpinionOf` is not a read.** `Pawn_RelationsTracker.cs:592` -\u003e\n`thoughts.TotalOpinionOffset` -\u003e `SituationalThoughtHandler.AppendSocialThoughts`\n(`:90`) -\u003e `CheckRecalculateSocialThoughts` (`:142`), which **creates a\n`CachedSocialThoughts` entry for the (observer, other) pair if none exists**\n(`:147-148`), instantiates `Thought_SituationalSocial` objects (`:169`), and\nstamps `lastQueryTick` (`:94`) — which feeds `Expired` and therefore keeps cache\nentries alive that would otherwise be reaped. Throttled to once per 100 ticks per\npair, so the FIRST call for a new pair is the expensive, mutating one.\nCost is dominated by `GetRelations` (`PawnRelationUtility.cs:11-42`), which runs\n`PawnRelationWorker_Kin` -\u003e `FamilyByBlood` -\u003e **a full family-graph BFS**.\n**Do not loop `OpinionOf` over N pawns — that is N full BFS walks.**\n\n**3. `PawnRelationUtility.GetMostImportantRelation` (`:44-55`) is the accessor to\nuse for \"what is X to Y\"** — no writes at all, exactly one `GetRelations` walk,\nand it is what vanilla uses for letters and the Social tab. Strictly cheaper than\n`OpinionOf`. Do NOT use `GetMostImportantColonyRelative` (`:187-206`) — it runs\nthat against every free colonist and prisoner on every map.\n\n\n`timetable.times` / `GetAssignment` (but `times` is the LIVE list — copy it; and\n`GetAssignment` has an **unguarded index**, 0..23 or it throws); every\n`Pawn_PlayerSettings` scalar (`medCare`, `hostilityResponse`, `selfTend`,\n`followDrafted`/`followFieldwork`, `animalsReleased`, `joinTick`); every\n`Pawn_GuestTracker` field plus `IsPrisoner`/`IsSlave`/`GuestStatus`/\n`HostFaction`/`Resistance`; the `Pawn.Is*` classification predicates;\n`relations.DirectRelations` / `GetFirstDirectRelationPawn` /\n`DirectRelationExists` / `RelatedToAnyoneOrAnyoneRelatedToMe`;\n`GetFirstSpouse`/`GetMother`/`GetFather`; `SocialCardUtility.GetPawnSituationLabel`;\n`Pawn.Name`/`gender`/`kindDef`; `ageTracker.AgeBiologicalYears` /\n`AgeChronologicalYears` (pure arithmetic); `story.Childhood`/`Adulthood`;\n`story.traits.allTraits` (the real backing list — copy, don't retain);\n`pawn.Ideo`.\n\n\n- **Null trackers.** `pawn.timetable` is null for anything not player-faction\n  humanlike (`PawnComponentsUtility.cs:296-299`). `pawn.playerSettings` is null\n  unless player faction / prisoner-of-player / on a holding platform (`:354-357`).\n  `pawn.ideo` exists for every humanlike regardless of DLC (`:104-107`) but\n  `ideo.Ideo` is null without Ideology — guard on `ModsConfig.IdeologyActive`\n  FIRST, `pawn.Ideo != null` second.\n- **`TimeAssignmentDefOf.Meditate` is null without Royalty**; the tracker scrubs\n  it to `Anything` on load (`Pawn_TimetableTracker.cs:38-48`).\n- **Restrict-tab label** is `AreaUtility.AreaAllowedLabel(pawn)`\n  (`Verse/AreaUtility.cs:42-49`), reading `AreaRestrictionInPawnCurrentMap`\n  (`:85-94`) — the null-guarded one. NOT the Effective variant.\n- **`Pawn.IsPrisonerOfColony` (`Pawn.cs:624`) dereferences `guest.HostFaction`\n  unguarded** — NRE if a pawn is `GuestStatus.Prisoner` with a null host faction.\n- **Work-tab column order** is generated, not XML: `PawnColumnDefGenerator.cs:30-45`\n  over `WorkTypeDefsUtility.WorkTypeDefsInPriorityOrder`. Net left-to-right =\n  `naturalPriority` DESCENDING, filtered to `def.visible`. Use the plain\n  `def.visible` field, not `VisibleCurrently`.\n- **`GuestStatus` is only `{Guest, Prisoner, Slave}`** — it does NOT encode\n  \"visitor\"; `Pawn.GuestStatus` returns null for a plain visitor with no host\n  faction. A classification ladder is needed, tightest-first, and\n  `IsFreeNonSlaveColonist` (`Pawn.cs:542`) is the tightest \"real colonist\".\n- `resistance`/`will` are **sentinel `-1f` until initialized** — `-1` means \"not\n  yet a prisoner\", not \"zero resistance\".\n- `LabelCap` embeds **rich-text colour markup** (Colorize on the backstory\n  title). For LLM output prefer `Name.ToStringShort` or `LabelShortCap`. Neither\n  is cached — fresh string per call — so compute once per pass.\n- `IsQuestLodger` clears/refills the static `tmpQuestWorkDisabled`\n  (`QuestUtility.cs:170`) and walks every quest part. Call once per pawn, never\n  in a loop.\n\n\nI verified independently, earlier this session, the class of hazard this rests\non: `MapPawns.FreeColonistsSpawned` really does clear and rebuild a shared list\non every access, and `DangerWatcher.DangerRating` really does re-enter it. Those\nare the same shape as the findings above and they were both real. I have NOT\nre-verified the specific line numbers here. Whoever takes 2.2 should check each\none it relies on — the citations are precise enough to make that cheap.","files":null}]}